                        "sense_id": "4a9e4ad7-0a94-39ec-9255-9c64b4f0d93c",
                        "entry_id": "3dc71c93-6800-39e5-bfc2-371bc3e9b678",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A liking for black people."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "offensive",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9af88de6-ca6c-4960-bf38-582ba9495618",
                                "sense_id": "4a9e4ad7-0a94-39ec-9255-9c64b4f0d93c",
                                "text": "The only trouble with this negrophilism is that it doesn't recognize the Negro as a man. It recognizes him only as a Negro—if sometimes as a Negro Jesus Christ. And that is the worst condescension of all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73c5c09d-3ed7-44cb-909d-38a6c323dabb",
                                "sense_id": "4a9e4ad7-0a94-39ec-9255-9c64b4f0d93c",
                                "text": "His negrophilism seems to be nothing beyond a fashion statement, almost a way of accessorizing. It's black pride without ever having to endure the downsides of being black."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
